          "final_text_tail": "thin the limit, a warning is logged and cleanup is abandoned (graceful degradation, exit stack reset so the context stays reusable). If cleanup finishes in time, any callback exception still propagates as before; the no-timeout path is byte-for-byte the old behavior. `logging` is imported lazily inside the method so `import click` stays light (satisfies `tests/test_imports.py`); `threading` is already on the light-import allowlist.\n  - Docstrings updated (`:param cleanup_timeout:`, `versionadded:: 8.2`, `close()` note).\n\n- `src/click/shell_completion.py`: the in-tree change closes contexts created while resolving completion args (`with` blocks in `_resolve_context`), so their `close()` cleanup now runs \u2014 and is bounded by `cleanup_timeout`, which flows through `ctx_args` \u2192 `make_context` \u2192 `Context`, and via parent inheritance to nested contexts.\n\n- `CHANGES.rst`: entry added under 8.2.0 Unreleased.\n\nVerified: default `None`/stored value, `ValueError` for `0`/`-1`/`\"x\"`, hanging callback + `cleanup_timeout=0.5` returns in ~0.5s with a logged warning, fast callbacks still run, exceptions still propagate, `context_settings={\"cleanup_timeout\": \u2026}`, `main(..., cleanup_timeout=\u2026)`/`runner.invoke(..., cleanup_timeout=\u2026)` completion returns in ~1s instead of hanging while still producing correct completions. (Note: running the suite needs `-W \"ignore::pytest.PytestRemovedIn10Warning\"` due to a pre-existing pytest-version incompatibility in `test_basic.py`, unrelated to this change.)",
